<title>UK: UK power firms to set up anti-law suit fund - paper.</title>
<headline>UK power firms to set up anti-law suit fund - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eight British electricity companies are planning to set up an eight million stg fund to fight legal claims that electronic magnetic fields generated by power lines are hazardous to health, a newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Financial Times reported that the companies, which are said to include National Grid Group Plc, South Western Electricity Plc and London Electricity Plc, are advised to create a company in the Channel island of Guernsey to fund potential costs arising from legal actions.</p>
<p>Five cases are pending against the UK power industry for the alleged harmful effects of electric magnetic fields, the FT said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
